;
SHUTDOWN, BACKUP AND UPDATES

A - Stopping the RCP/M
B - Backing up and restoring
C - Updating the system
:A
STOPPING THE RCP/M

BYE logs off a caller, not the whole machine.
Let a caller finish and save any work. Between calls, use local
Ctrl-C at BYE's menu prompt, then RETURN to enter ordinary CP/M.
At private local CP/M, enter:

    SYSUTLS:BYEBYE

Wait for the emulator to stop before copying or editing images.
A blanked caller or idle listener does not mean the guest is stopped.
:B
BACKING UP AND RESTORING

Copy the complete stopped installation to separate storage.
Include disks/, library volumes, uploads/inbox/, state/, RCPM.CONF
and private SYSOP.DOC. Protect backup credentials and mail.

Restore into a new directory from a complete snapshot, not pieces
of unrelated backups. Stop the original before using its port.
A second copy on the same disk is not protection against disk loss.
:C
UPDATING THE SYSTEM

Do not unpack a fresh release over a working board. Test it in
a separate directory and follow that release's migration instructions.
Preserve your accounts, messages, permissions, uploads and custom
software. Keep emulator and BYE driver versions matched.

Service installation, scheduled backups and monitoring are covered
by separate host administration documentation.
